WEBVTT

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.290
Is this it?

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:17.120
Yeah.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.750
St. Pierre’s Tokyo Main Branch.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.500
Let’s cut loose.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.350
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.220
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.520
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.890
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:45.980
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.750
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:07.130
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:15.110
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:22.940
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:30.700
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:38.170
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:47.550
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:56.310
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.570
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.520
is the light of only you.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:07.310
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:12.120
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:19.840
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.080
Close Attack!!

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.050
The birth of the Black <i>Japan</i>!

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:33.000
There’s just one reason for having you come
all the way from St. Pierre’s Kyushu Branch...

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.850
The Pantasia Southern Tokyo Branch,
which is diagonally opposite us...

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:41.760
I want you to thoroughly crush them.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.720
Is this the enemy’s diet bread?

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:50.230
It appears that they are using nanshoukasei wheat flour.

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:53.860
If it’s just this, we can make as many as you like.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:56.610
We can choose whatever method we like, right?

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.610
Yes, of course.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:01.610
However, it still remains inscrutable.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.410
We’re people from St. Pierre.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:09.460
Therefore, why would you,
from Pantasia, want to use us?

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.130
That’s true...

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:15.000
On top of that, we’re trying to crush that store.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.630
We would like to hear a reason that satisfies us.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.010
That’s true...

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.890
Oh, shut up. There’s no reason.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:27.850
I guess the reason would be that... I love bread.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.770
I’m just harassing them
because I hate and despise them.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:33.770
You got a problem with it?

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.410
Everyone who loves bread is... family!

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.780
It shouldn’t matter whether
they’re from Pantasia or St. Pierre.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:45.410
However...

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.740
It’s just that the Southern Tokyo Branch is different.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.290
How is it different?

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.290
They...

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.260
They...

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:02.550
They mixed enzymes that digest
protein, endoproteases, into my dough...

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.970
and laughed at the fact that my
dough wouldn’t ferment, no matter what.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:09.970
The yeast that I had lovingly cultured,
and many years worth of my research...

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.820
were bombed by them.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.580
They scattered my deceased
mother’s ashes onto a dead tree.

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:21.410
How cruel...

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:23.120
They’re like demons.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:24.490
Is this true?

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.380
I’m a woman who’s like white snow...

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:31.670
Please believe me, Azusagawa Yukino.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.380
Whatever...

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:36.180
Actually, all of that was done by me!

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:45.470
The owner, Kirisaki, has agreed to cooperate with me.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:49.890
That’s why I thought of having you lend me a hand...

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.600
I understand.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.000
Leave the rest to us.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.080
We’ll be sure to take your revenge.

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:02.200
What simple-minded morons.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:09.660
The owner, Kirisaki, told me to
leave the cockroaches alone...

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.660
but I definitely won’t leave them alone.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:14.160
Definitely not.

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:24.390
It is me.

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:27.650
I see.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.610
So, St. Pierre has called upon the three of them...

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:32.520
All right.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:34.860
Please continue to stay there and keep watch.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:44.400
I wonder how the Southern Tokyo
Branch will face up to this trial...

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:48.280
Hmm... I wonder what happened...

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:53.290
It’s usually so busy at this time
that I have to make clones of myself...

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:57.170
Azuma.

00:05:57.170 --> 00:06:00.790
Shouldn’t you start getting
things ready for your trip to France?

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:03.100
I <i>am</i> getting ready.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:09.800
I have to ready plenty of sauce for
<i>Japan</i> #57, for when I’m not here.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:13.510
As usual, all he’s thinking about is bread.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.310
We’re in trouble, everyone!

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:23.980
St. Pierre has started selling the
same nanshoukasei diet bread as ours.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.320
I see...

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:26.940
So that’s how they’ve decided to go...

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.410
I had expected this to a certain degree,

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:31.880
but to think that it’d be so soon...

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.120
Everyone! There’s something terrible happening!

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.420
We know.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:38.080
St. Pierre’s selling the diet bread, right?

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:40.800
What... You already knew, eh?

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:42.960
Kawachi-san...

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.670
You keep coming here,

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.980
but are things okay over at the Main Branch?

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.100
Since I’m leaving for France soon,
the Main Branch gave me a vacation.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:52.850
However, that doesn’t mean
that you have to come here.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.180
He really must have no other place to go.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:58.180
So, what are you going to do?

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.030
This is troublesome.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:04.530
At this rate, much of the diet bread will remain unsold.

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:05.940
It’s all right.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:11.200
We can just turn all the unsold bread
into the <i>Japan</i> #57 kabukiage bread.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.290
You moron!

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:14.160
Doing that won’t solve the problem!

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:16.160
Everyone! We’re in trouble!

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.670
Everybody already knows.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:21.170
St. Pierre’s making the diet bread, right?

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:22.750
That’s true, but...

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.170
The television,
please turn on the television.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.220
Here at St. Pierre’s Tokyo Main Branch,

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:33.680
they have taken this opportunity and finally
announced their newly developed bread.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:34.220
Diet

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:37.640
Apparently, they use a special
wheat flour that is high in hard fiber.
Diet

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:38.900
Apparently, they use a special
wheat flour that is high in hard fiber.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:43.650
This is hard for the stomach and
intestine to digest, and is optimal for dieting.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:48.540
This looks like it’ll gain
enormous popularity among young girls.

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:50.070
May I?

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.370
Uh, sure.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:56.250
It appears that there’s a similar bread
being made at a bakery in the neighborhood.

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:58.870
That bread is a complete fake.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:01.670
Everyone, please be careful not to be fooled.

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:03.550
Hey, bakery from the neighborhood!

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:05.510
If you have a problem with it, bring it on.

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:07.420
We’ll take you on anytime.

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:09.630
Most likely,

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:12.730
they figured out how to use
autodigestion in the recipe, too.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.980
We really cannot underestimate them.

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:16.980
But, hey!

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:20.110
The fakes aren’t ours, but theirs, right?

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:21.610
Although that may be the truth,

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:25.240
they are speaking with a lot of
financial backing behind them.

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:26.940
Even black will become white.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.940
Black will become white...?

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:31.740
At this rate, if we continue
staying like this with our arms folded,

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:35.280
Pantasia will be taken over, just as Yukino wants.

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:38.030
We need to come up with a plan against this.

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:40.540
Kanmuri...

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.540
How about a bread that’s good for your health?

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.800
If it’s a bread that’s both delicious and good for you,

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:48.250
any customer would be happy.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.260
Delicious, and good for your health...

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.310
That’s true,

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:56.270
but it’s more like a dream...

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:58.850
It’s <i>Japan</i> #56!

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.770
I’m sure it’ll go well with that.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.770
T-That’s the one from that time, isn’t it?

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:04.860
That’s right.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.190
It’s from that time.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:09.770
It’s the bread that I first tried to make
during the Main Branch Employment Exam.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:12.780
If you’re talking about <i>Japan</i> #56, then...

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:16.750
The dough for that bread, which I spoiled...

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:18.710
which you had to give up on making, in the end...

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:19.840
That bread, right?

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:25.160
That was an unfortunate accident.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.050
T-That’s right!

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:28.670
It was an unfortunate accident...

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:30.020
Azuma-san...

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:31.470
Come to think of it,

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:36.970
why did you go ahead and make <i>Japan</i> #57, the
kabukiage bread, instead of <i>Japan</i> #56 after that?

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:40.570
Because at that time, I had
used up all of the ingredients.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:42.810
But...

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.980
If I get my sister to bring them,
I could make it right away.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:48.980
Exactly what ingredients do you intend to use?

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:50.490
Rice bran.

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:51.020
Rice...

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:52.080
Bran?

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:56.820
Is it the rice bran that you
use for nukazuke and nukamiso?

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:58.320
That’s right!

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:01.870
It’s true that neither white nor brown rice is as

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.890
balanced in its nutritional content as rice bran.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:10.300
If works to expel dioxins that
have accumulated in the body.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:10.790
It has been called the natural health product of dreams.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:13.340
Natural health product of dreams

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.100
That’s amazing!

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:18.090
In that case, we might win
against St. Pierre´s diet bread.

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:19.930
However,

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:22.810
rice bran normally has a peculiar bitterness to it.

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:25.100
It isn’t used for anything other
than in fertilizer, or for pickling.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.600
You need to develop quite some
trick to be able to add it to bread.

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:30.530
It’s all right.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:35.120
By mixing Grandfather’s freshly
harvested, new breed of rice bran

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:39.360
with my special dough,
you’ll get a bread that isn’t bitter.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.570
Freshly harvested new breed, eh?

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:44.080
Just as I thought...

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:45.580
What’s wrong?

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:46.840
Umm...

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:49.090
Azuma-san, I believe that your home is in...

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:50.800
It’s in Niigata.

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:53.300
You can harvest the very best rice there.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:56.090
Can you harvest the new breed,
even in this season?

00:10:58.140 --> 00:10:59.340
That’s right...

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:01.020
That’s true...

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:03.350
Well, let’s just wait until fall then.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:05.100
We can’t wait that long!

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:06.350
It’s over, isn’t it?

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:11.740
Hey, Azuma.

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:14.660
Could we use this instead of rice bran?

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:19.360
It is partly my fault that
<i>Japan</i> #56 remained incomplete.

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:23.120
With this, I’d like to atone for my sin a little bit.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.870
What’s that?

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:29.840
It’s the secret ingredient of a healthy
bread that my father tried to create.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:36.340
My father was a man who constantly fussed
over the dinner bread that we ate every day.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.970
Moreover, since we’d eat it everyday,

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:41.840
he’d mix in things that were good for our health.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:42.430
Medicinal Herb Bread

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.860
He’d say that he wanted to
revolutionize the bread industry.

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:46.850
Medicinal Herb Bread

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:49.990
In the end, his dream did not materialize.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:53.650
However, I’ve wanted to perfect it someday.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.860
So, I always carry it around,
close to my skin.

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:01.860
We’re going to use something black
like that as an ingredient in bread?

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.500
I guess it’s impossible, then...

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:08.870
Despite saying that it’s good for health,
in the end, it was something that failed...

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:10.580
No, it’s all right.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:12.630
Huh?

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.720
With this, we can do it.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:18.130
A good-for-your-health <i>Japan</i> #56.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:19.590
For real?

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:22.340
Can we win against St. Pierre with that?

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:23.560
Yeah.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:25.930
If they turned black into white...

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:29.890
then we’ll just have to turn white into black!

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:47.750
Let’s go.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:48.250
Okay.

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:49.490
All right.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.670
Well, lookie here.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:00.500
If it isn’t the folk from the
bakery diagonally opposite ours.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.510
What do you want?

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:06.140
Could it be that you’ve abandoned your store,

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:09.010
and decided to apply for work here?

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:10.520
Umm...

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:11.690
You see...

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:15.360
Well, since you said, “If you
have a problem with it, bring it on”...

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.650
We’ll take you up on that.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:19.280
We challenge you.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:22.650
Here’s the Improved <i>Japan</i> #56:
Black <i>Japan</i>!

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:26.870
W-What’s this black thing?

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:29.290
I’ve never seen such a bread.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:32.040
You really want us to eat this thing?

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:35.210
If you eat this and think that it’s delicious,

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:39.250
we’ll have you take back calling us fake on television.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:41.470
We don’t really mind.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:44.010
And, if it doesn’t taste good?

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:48.150
In that case, we’ll shut down the
Pantasia Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:50.310
That sounds interesting.

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:52.020
Yeah, it’ll save us the trouble.

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:55.780
Well then, let’s eat some right away.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.310
This slight fragrance is...

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:02.860
It’s bamboo, the smell of bamboo!

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:05.360
Why, from such a bread...?

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:14.830
What...

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:15.330
the...

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.340
T-This is...

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:27.800
Oh, this is...

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.280
P-Princess Kaguya!

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:36.730
Grandpa,

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.810
please take care of me from now on.

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:44.820
Several years later...

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:52.240
Please marry me, Princess Kaguya.

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:54.120
Don’t wanna!

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:56.330
H-How cruel!

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:17.150
Grandpa, Grandma,

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:19.230
I’ll return to the moon.

00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:21.030
What was that?

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:23.450
After having raised you for so many years? No way!

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:24.870
That’s cruel.

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.120
Oh, shut up.

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:28.080
I’m the Princess of the Moon.

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:31.300
I’m not a woman who’d spend
all her life in a place like this.

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:34.710
See ya!

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:36.620
H-How cruel!

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:51.430
We must save the princess and take
her back to Earth at all costs!

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:53.440
We have detected the presence of a Giant Colony there.

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:54.060
There it is!

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:55.350
That’s where the princess is.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.490
Oh, Princess!

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:17.740
We’ve come to get you.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:22.590
